Update my existing Node.js backend into a clean **stateless Groww bridge backend**.

## MAIN ARCHITECTURE

The backend is ONLY a bridge between my Flutter app and Groww.

```text
Flutter
    ↓
https://api.my-domain.com/v1/...
    ↓
Node.js Backend
    ↓
https://api.groww.in/v1/...
    ↓
Groww
```

The Flutter API path should match the Groww API path wherever possible.

Example:

```text
Flutter:
POST https://api.my-domain.com/v1/order/create

Backend:
POST https://api.groww.in/v1/order/create
```

The backend must receive the Flutter request, call the corresponding Groww API, and return the Groww response.

## IMPORTANT

Do NOT create a universal `/proxy` endpoint.

Do NOT accept arbitrary `targetUrl` from Flutter.

Do NOT create a database.

Do NOT permanently save:

* Groww access token
* Groww API key
* Groww TOTP token
* Groww TOTP secret
* broker credentials
* order history
* user credentials

Everything must remain stateless.

The backend only holds request data in memory while processing the request.

Never log tokens, API keys, secrets, Authorization headers, or sensitive request bodies.

