# GROWW TOKEN API

## 3. Generate Groww Access Token

Flutter calls:

```text
POST /v1/token/api/access
```

Backend calls:

```text
POST https://api.groww.in/v1/token/api/access
```

The backend should forward the required request body and headers.

Example Flutter request:

```json
{
  "key_type": "totp",
  "totp": "123456"
}
```

The backend must:

1. Receive the request.
2. Forward it to Groww.
3. Return Groww's response.
4. Never save the generated access token.
5. Never log the TOTP.
6. Never log the Authorization header.

---

# GROWW ORDER API

## 4. Create Order

Flutter:

```text
POST /v1/order/create
```

Backend:

```text
POST https://api.groww.in/v1/order/create
```

Example request:

```json
{
  "trading_symbol": "TCS",
  "quantity": 3,
  "price": 2105,
  "validity": "DAY",
  "exchange": "NSE",
  "segment": "CASH",
  "product": "MIS",
  "order_type": "LIMIT",
  "transaction_type": "BUY",
  "order_reference_id": "RMA-123456"
}
```

The Flutter request will contain the Groww Authorization header:

```text
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>
```

The backend must forward the Authorization header to Groww.

Do not save it.

Do not log it.

Do not modify the order data unless required by Groww.

